concept:crimes-amendment-enforcement-of-fines-act-1998-sch-1-sec-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1 Subsection 3B(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-1 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1) The Governor-General may make arrangements with the Governor of a State, the Government of the Australian Capital Territory, the Administrator of the Northern Territory or the Administrator of Norfolk Island for:  (a) officers of the State or Territory to exercise powers and perform functions; and  (b) facilities and procedures of the State or Territory to be made available; in relation to the carrying out or enforcement under this Act of orders made under this Act or another Act." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1) The Governor-General may make arrangements with the Governor of a State, the Government of the Australian Capital Territory, the Administrator of the Northern Territory or the Administrator of Norfolk Island for:  (a) officers of the State or Territory to exercise powers and perform functions; and  (b) facilities and procedures of the State or Territory to be made available; in relation to the carrying out or enforcement under this Act of orders made under this Act or another Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7bcb232b3d317444994faad76e43fa21af63abffbd7e9df6d14b91828833afdc" ;
    cof:pageNumber "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Arrange with states and territories for officers to exercise powers and perform functions." ;
